
<p>Zac Hall, 9to5Mac:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>macOS 27 Golden Gate beta 6 introduces redesigned traffic light window controls. The new look resembles older Mac OS X systems with more detail in each button.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>Nice. But these changes can’t improve fast enough for me — I am impatient. The MacOS user interface had been in a slow, steady, sad, no-fun decline for years, and then, a year ago, the bottom fell out with the disaster of 26 Tahoe.</p>

<p>But <em>all</em> the changes in 27 Golden Gate are in the right direction. Golden Gate is not a mixed bag. Designers with taste and talent are clearly <a href="https://daringfireball.net/linked/2026/08/12/nature-is-healing">back at the helm</a>. And I love that they’re still pushing UI and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/10/ios-27-beta-5-icons/">icon</a> changes in mid-August, entering <a href="https://daringfireball.net/linked/2026/08/10/ios-27-beta-5">the home stretch</a> of the .0 beta cycle.</p>

